%T A130536 66977,29,31,149057,613,37,761,41,43,1013,47,1201,1301,53,1146097
%N A130536 Prime numbers arising from A057856.
%C A130536 Conjecture: For all pairs of relative prime numbers (x, y) there exists at least one number n = 2^m and one prime number p such that p = x^n + y^n. This sequence shows one case of this conjecture where y = x + 1.
%C A130536 The conjecture for arbitrary coprime positive integers x and y is false. Take x = 8 and y = 27. For every integer r >= 1, 8^r + 27^r = (2^r + 3^r)*(4^r - 6^r + 9^r), with both factors greater than 1. In particular, 8^(2^m) + 27^(2^m) is composite for every integer m >= 0. This does not refute the special case y = x + 1. See also A057856. - _Eiver Rodríguez_, Oct 01 2026
%e A130536 a(10)=2211377674535255285545615254209921 because A057856(10)=32 and 2211377674535255285545615254209921 = 10^32 + 11^32 = 100000000000000000000000000000000 + 2111377674535255285545615254209921.
%o A130536 (PARI) a(n) = my(k=1); while (!isprime(p=(n+1)^k + n^k), k++); p; \\ _Michel Marcus_, Sep 16 2018
